%% Article 02 - Commit to deploy sequence
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Author (Fabric)
    participant W as Ved-Development
    participant G as Azure DevOps repo
    participant P as Pipeline
    participant D as detect_changes.py
    participant E as deploy_fabric_workspace.py
    participant T as Ved-UAT

    A->>W: author item
    W->>G: commit to fabric-workspaces/Ved (develop)
    G->>P: trigger
    P->>D: checkout fetchDepth 0, run detection
    D->>D: resolve baseline from shape of HEAD
    D->>D: classify each changed path
    D-->>P: ved=true, fin=false, hr=false
    Note over P: FIN and HR stages evaluate false and are Skipped.<br/>They receive zero Fabric API calls.

    P->>P: branch = develop, so validate only
    P->>E: SOLUTION_KEY=ved, environment=DEV, VALIDATE_ONLY=true
    E->>E: resolve source, reject repo root, assert non-empty
    E-->>P: validated, no workspace changes

    Note over G,T: Human merges develop into release
    G->>P: trigger on release
    P->>D: detection re-runs on the merge commit
    D-->>P: ved=true
    P->>E: SOLUTION_KEY=ved, environment=UAT, VALIDATE_ONLY=false
    E->>E: guards pass, resolve $(VED_UAT_WORKSPACE_ID)
    E->>T: unpublish orphans, then publish all items
    T-->>P: success
    P->>P: Summary stage reports the matrix
